omx-dsp (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version 0.19.0: the mix module's bus sum, analyser tap, load meter and
    gain-reduction reading (#98)
  * meter: the gain-reduction step's comment counts its three powf and says
    why a 0 ms release lands at once (#98)
  * mix golden: log10f is the correctly rounded omx_log10f, so the gr digests
    hold on every glibc (#98)
  * Bus sum and load meter digests written by the engine's copies, the
    identity check and their sabotages (#98)
  * Mix module: the real-time load meter's measure half (#98)
  * Mix module: one source's contribution to a summing bus, as entries of the
    mix matrix (#98)
  * mix: the analyser tap's header states the facts, with no private paths
    (#98)
  * Analyser tap digests written by the engine's copies, the identity check
    and two sabotages (#98)
  * Mix module: one analyser tap's reading, the mono sum, one spectrum and
    the three-stage low zoom (#98)
  * Peak hold and gain-reduction digests written by the engine's copies, the
    identity check and a sabotage of each (#98)
  * Mix module: the meters' peak hold and the gain-reduction reading's hold
    and recovery (#98)
  * mix-engine-identity: the installed omx-contract, nothing downloaded, and
    omx_gen.h forwards to the engine's generators (#98)
  * ci: the shared release workflow also reads the run it reports on
    (actions: read)
  * ci: the dry-run job allows the issue-opening step of the shared release
    workflow
  * release: allow the shared workflow to open an issue when a release fails

